1
00:00:01,530 --> 00:00:09,180
So in our previous section we have seen how to update Mifare classic card using ACR 1 to 2 tool.

2
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:18,020
In this section we are going to update the same Mifare classic card, but using this MFC 5 to 2 STM

3
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:19,500
eight microcontroller.

4
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:23,880
So this is the board we are going to use.

5
00:00:23,910 --> 00:00:30,090
So it has the same chip which we have used before in our earlier sections.

6
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:32,369
The MFC 5 to 2 Chip.

7
00:00:32,369 --> 00:00:37,050
But this board also contains this STM chip over here.

8
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:39,450
This STM microcontroller.

9
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:47,820
So first we will program this STM eight microcontroller and using this microcontroller, we will operate

10
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:56,370
this MFC 5 to 2 Chip and we will read, write and update data using this STM eight microcontroller.

11
00:00:56,760 --> 00:01:02,470
So to operate on this board, we need two other things as well.

12
00:01:02,710 --> 00:01:09,340
The first thing we need is USB to TTL cable, which is over here in Silver Color, you can see.

13
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:17,620
And the other thing is STM eight and Stm32 USB, which you can easily purchase from Amazon or AliExpress.

14
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:23,200
So all these things you can easily purchase from Amazon or AliExpress.

15
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:25,540
These are the tools which we are going to use.

16
00:01:25,570 --> 00:01:30,490
Now let me just go through the cost of these tools real quick.

17
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:35,970
So the cost of hardware MFC 5 to 2 with STM microcontroller.

18
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:40,690
This is the board which we are going to use and it will cost you around 4 to $5.

19
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:50,830
Then USB two cable, we will use USB two cable to operate on Mifare classic card and we will use STM

20
00:01:50,830 --> 00:01:57,290
eight and Stm32 USB, which is the same USB for STM eight and stm32.

21
00:01:57,310 --> 00:02:05,370
This is the USB over here and we will use this USB to program our STM eight microcontroller.

22
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:06,340
Right.

23
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:15,080
So this is the cost of USB two cable, then STM eight and STM 32 USB will cost you around 3 to $5.

24
00:02:15,090 --> 00:02:22,950
So the complete cost of all these hardware is around $10, which is quite less than 1 to 2 module,

25
00:02:22,950 --> 00:02:25,260
which was around 25 to $30.

26
00:02:25,410 --> 00:02:34,680
So these are the hardware requirements and the both the softwares for this tool are free.

27
00:02:34,950 --> 00:02:37,320
So you can easily download these two software.

28
00:02:37,350 --> 00:02:43,830
The first one is STB, which is a software to program STM eight microcontroller.

29
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:52,890
And the other tool is MFC 5 to 2, which is a software we will use to, you know, update our Mifare

30
00:02:52,890 --> 00:02:54,190
classic card through this software.

31
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:57,150
So make sure you download these two softwares as well.

